# 1. Project Identity & Strategic Context

**Freshness: High - recently verified in this session.**

Dwell Docket is Lane 14's accepted app for small-carrier and dispatcher
after-the-fact detention reconciliation. One stop CSV becomes a local docket of
unrecovered, evidence-gap, recovered, no-detention, and invalid rows. Success
means one screen, one input surface, one oversized action, browser-local
processing, downloadable output, no credentials, and no unsupported commercial
claim.

The repository is
`/Users/fortunevieyra/Documents/Github/ai-projects/factory-apps/lane-14/dwell-docket`
on `main`. The public target is
`https://github.com/ownasquare/dwell-docket`. Node 22+, vanilla ESM, a minimal
static server, Node test runner, TypeScript checkJs analysis, Prettier, and
Playwright are used. Runtime dependencies are zero.

# 2. Current System State & Architecture Map

**Freshness: High - recently verified in this session.**

Implemented flow:

`CSV -> File.text -> src/csv.js -> src/detention.js -> src/app.js -> DOM + Blob download`

Working:

